{"id": "4d57bd09-953d-4c6e-a3d5-252afce3f659", "timestamp": "2026-11-11T07:01:57.057989", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "call_9b25bdac35f447dbb514735c", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "=== /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T1.md\n# Task: `check-anchors` misses a deleted OpenTimestamps proof\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Bug report from an outside verifier:** in a ledger whose entries are covered by Sigstore range attestations, they deleted the OpenTimestamps proof file of a range head (for example `anchors/000002.ots`, where `anchors/000002.sigstore.json` attests the range ending at entry 2). Afterwards `python3 record/record.py check-anchors` still exited 0, so the missing proof went unreported.\n\n**Required behaviour:**\n- `check-anchors` must exit 1 when the `.ots` proof for any attested range head is missing.\n- It must print a message to stderr containing `NNNNNN.ots is missing` (for example `000002.ots is missing`).\n- With the proof present, the existing behaviour must not change.\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`.\n=== /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T3.md\n# Task: make a stuck OpenTimestamps proof visible\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Background:** a scheduled job that completes pending OpenTimestamps proofs failed silently for five days. Nothing noticed, because `check-anchors` treats a pending proof (one not yet confirmed in Bitcoin) as acceptable.\n\n**Required:** add an opt-in option `--max-pending-hours H` to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors`.\n- Without the option, behaviour is unchanged: pending proofs are still accepted (exit 0).\n- With the option, if any range head's proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago, exit 1. Print to stderr a message containing `still pending N h`, where N is the whole number of hours since the attestation (for example `still pending 72 h`).\n- A pending proof younger than H hours is fine (exit 0).\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`.\n=== /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/PREREG.md\n# Pre-registration: bench-1, OpenHands with free models on exagium's past fixes\n\nWritten 2026-11-11 before any run. Author: Claude Opus (it chose the tasks, wrote the statements and the grader, and is not an arm). Changes after the first run need a new pre-registration.\n\n## Questions\n- **H1.** Is OpenHands, run headless, a workable base for the machine and harness?\n- **H2.** Can free models drive it to fix real exagium bugs?\n- **Budget.** How many model calls does a task take? That number decides whether the free allowance (1,000 OpenRouter requests a day) carries agent work.\n- **H5.** What memory does a run need, and would it fit Oracle's free 12 GB?\n\n## Tasks (`tasks.json`, statements in `tasks/`)\nEach is a past fix in this repo that added its own test:\n\n| Task | Fix commit | What it adds |\n|---|---|---|\n| T1 | `4711b86` | `check-anchors` reports a missing `.ots` proof |\n| T2 | `06bc550` | `_orphan_entries_problem` |\n| T3 | `bdd7ec5` | `check-anchors --max-pending-hours` |\n\nHow each task is set up and graded:\n- The agent gets the tree at the commit **before** the fix, as a fresh git repo with no history, plus the task statement.\n- **Validity, checked before registering:** each hidden test fails on the base and passes on the fix.\n- **Grading, by script only (`grade.py`):** the fix commit's test file is copied over the agent's own. The task passes if the hidden test passes **and** no test in `p2p-<fix>.json` fails. Those are the tests that passed both before and after the real fix.\n\n## Arms (each provider's default settings, one run per task, 9 runs)\n| Arm | Model | Provider |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` | OpenRouter |\n| B | `recursive/flint-v1.0:free` | OpenRouter, built for coding agents |\n| C | `gemini-3.8-flash` | Google AI Studio free tier |\n\n- The OpenHands CLI is the latest at run time; its version is recorded.\n- Each run is capped at 25 minutes of wall time.\n- A paid OpenRouter model makes the job fail before it runs.\n\n## Measures, per run\n- Pass or fail (hidden test and pass-to-pass).\n- Steps and model calls, counted from OpenHands' JSON events.\n- Wall time and peak memory (`/usr/bin/time -v`).\n- Provider errors (429s and the like), recorded apart from model failures.\n- Diff size.\n- **Contamination flag:** if the event log mentions the fix commit's hash or this repo's GitHub URL, the run is reported separately. The repo is public, so an agent could look up the answer.\n\n## Decisions, fixed now\n- **H1 holds** if the harness completes at least 7 of 9 runs without a harness crash, whatever the model does.\n- **H2 holds** if at least one arm passes 2 of 3 tasks without contamination. **Fails** if no arm passes any.\n- **Budget:** report the median calls per task. If the median exceeds 100 calls, free OpenRouter supports at most about 10 tasks a day. That goes to the owner as a cost decision.\n- With 9 runs, every result is **a direction, not evidence.** No ranking of models is claimed.\n\n## Spend\n$0. All arms are free. The expected budget use is under 900 OpenRouter requests (two arms × 3 tasks × at most 150 calls) and under the Gemini free daily limit (unknown; a quota 429 is reported as \"unavailable\", never as a model failure).\n\n## Outside review before running (Nemotron 3 Ultra, 2026-11-11) and changes made\n1. **\"Fixes are in the models' training data.\"** Rebutted with dates. The fixes were committed 5–11 Nov 2026. Nemotron 3 Ultra was released 4 June 2026 and Flint on 21 Oct 2026, so neither could have seen them. Gemini 3.8 Flash's release date is unknown and is recorded as a caveat. Web lookup is still possible, so the contamination flag stays.\n2. **The H2 rule didn't cover every result.** It is now:\n   - **holds** if any arm passes 2 or more of 3, uncontaminated;\n   - **fails** if 0 of 9 pass;\n   - **inconclusive** otherwise.\n3. **\"Runners have 7 GB.\"** GitHub's standard public-repo Linux runners have 16 GB, so peak memory is measured below the cap. The cap is recorded with the result.\n4. **Grader not pinned.** Every result now records the repo commit, which pins `grade.py`, `tasks.json` and the `p2p` lists.\n5. **One run each.** Accepted: the result is a direction, as stated above.\n6. **Correlated 429s.** At most 2 jobs run in parallel. 429s are counted per run and reported beside wall time and calls.\n7. **OpenHands version.** Pinned to openhands-cli commit `283c6ac` (v1.16.0). Note: the CLI's README has marked it \"no longer actively maintained\" since Aug 2026, in favour of Agent Canvas. That is a finding for H1.\n8. **No control.** Added arm **Z**: no agent, grade the untouched base. It must fail all 3 tasks, or the grading is broken and the run is void.\n=== /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/grade.py\n\"\"\"Grade one agent attempt by hidden tests (SWE-bench style). Standard library only.\n\nusage: grade.py WORKDIR FIX_TEST_FILE HIDDEN_TEST [PASS_TO_PASS_JSON]\n\nCopies the fix commit's record/test_record.py over the agent's copy (so the agent can't\nedit the grading tests), runs every test in it with unittest, and prints one JSON object:\n  hidden: \"pass\" | \"fail\" | \"error\" | \"missing\"\n  pass_to_pass_broken: tests that passed on the original code but fail now\n  results: {test_id: outcome}\nExit 0 always; the verdict is in the JSON.\n\"\"\"\nimport json, os, shutil, subprocess, sys\n\nRUNNER = r'''\nimport json, sys, unittest\nsys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nsuite = unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromName(\"test_record\")\nout = {}\nclass R(unittest.TestResult):\n    def addSuccess(self, t): out[t.id().split(\".\")[-1]] = \"pass\"\n    def addFailure(self, t, e): out[t.id().split(\".\")[-1]] = \"fail\"\n    def addError(self, t, e): out[getattr(t, \"id\", lambda: str(t))().split(\".\")[-1]] = \"error\"\n    def addSkip(self, t, r): out[t.id().split(\".\")[-1]] = \"skip\"\nsuite.run(R())\nprint(\"@@RESULTS@@\" + json.dumps(out))\n'''\n\n\ndef run_tests(workdir, fix_test_file, timeout=900):\n    rec = os.path.join(workdir, \"record\")\n    shutil.copyfile(fix_test_file, os.path.join(rec, \"test_record.py\"))\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-c\", RUNNER], cwd=rec, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        return {\"_harness\": \"timeout\"}\n    for line in p.stdout.splitlines():\n        if line.startswith(\"@@RESULTS@@\"):\n            return json.loads(line[len(\"@@RESULTS@@\"):])\n    return {\"_harness\": \"no results\", \"_stderr\": p.stderr[-800:]}\n\n\ndef main():\n    workdir, fix_test_file, hidden = sys.argv[1:4]\n    p2p = json.load(open(sys.argv[4])) if len(sys.argv) > 4 else None\n    res = run_tests(workdir, fix_test_file)\n    broken = [t for t in (p2p or []) if res.get(t) != \"pass\"]\n    print(json.dumps({\"hidden\": res.get(hidden, \"missing\"), \"pass_to_pass_broken\": broken,\n                      \"n_tests\": len([k for k in res if not k.startswith(\"_\")]), \"results\": res}))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n=== /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks.json\n[\n {\"id\": \"T1\", \"base\": \"4711b86^\", \"fix\": \"4711b86\", \"hidden_test\": \"test_a_missing_ots_proof_for_a_range_head_is_caught\"},\n {\"id\": \"T2\", \"base\": \"06bc550^\", \"fix\": \"06bc550\", \"hidden_test\": \"test_orphans_must_publish_the_hidden_entries\"},\n {\"id\": \"T3\", \"base\": \"bdd7ec5^\", \"fix\": \"bdd7ec5\", \"hidden_test\": \"test_a_proof_left_pending_too_long_is_caught_only_when_asked\"}\n]"}], "is_error": false, "command": "for f in /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T1.md /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks/T3.md /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/PREREG.md /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/grade.py /home/runner/work/exagium/exagium/src/router/bench/tasks.json; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done", "exit_code": 0, "timeout": false, "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "runner", "hostname": "runnervm7aw5e", "working_dir": "/home/runner/work/exagium/exagium", "py_interpreter_path": "/usr/bin/python", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "full_output_save_dir": "/home/runner/.openhands/conversations/738f6895351f4632b1947bfc6419acac/observations", "kind": "TerminalObservation"}, "action_id": "8ef19974-bc7b-41d6-9f65-7524325468b2", "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
